{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1091419-variant-mysteries-of-the-flesh","id":1091419,"title":"[Variant] Mysteries of the Flesh","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-11T21:36:23-07:00","id":1091419,"title":"[Variant] Mysteries of the Flesh","content":"Under this rules-variant, Physical Disciplines are considered to be both normal Disciplines <i>and</i> Coils belonging to appropriately-named Mysteries. For most characters, this doesn't change anything. However, for members of the Ordo Dracul, this lends a few synergistic effects:<br /> <br /> \u2022 When purchasing a new dot of the Discipline, they may pay either the cost for a dot of the Discipline or a dot of the Coil, whichever would be lower. For example, a Daeva who has chosen to focus on the Mystery of Resilience could purchase Resilience dots for three XP each.<br /> <br /> \u2022 They may develop Scales for the Discipline, and may apply any other special modifications (such as Crucible) to it normally.<br /> <br /> \u2022 As an odd side effect, Strix that possess the bodies of Ordo members find that they do not gain the benefits of any of their host's Physical Disciplines. If they want to make the corpse they inhabit stronger, they must bring their own dots of Vigor.<br /> <br /> =---=<br /> <br /> Because the transvampirists deserve to be the best at pushing their flesh to the limits. Also, the idea of Celerity/Resilience/Vigor Scales is pretty darn cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T21:58:37-07:00","id":1091422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1091419-variant-mysteries-of-the-flesh#post1091419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, the idea of Celerity/Resilience/Vigor Scales is pretty darn cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would there be any difference between them and Celerity/Resilience/Vigor Devotions?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T22:17:46-07:00","id":1091426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-req